[0]
t=BMDC Executive Revision Level

[1]
t=Lo-Speed (below breakpoint) Acceleration
d=The amount by which velocity is increased at each iteration of the Interpolator if acceleration is required and velocity is below breakpoint.

[2]
t=Hi-Speed (above breakpoint) Acceleration
d=The amount by which velocity is increased at each iteration of the Interpolator if acceleration is required and velocity is above breakpoint.

[3]
t=Acceleration Break-Point
d=Velocity below which Low-Speed-Acceleration value is used and above which High-Speed-Acceleration value is used.

[4]
t=Deceleration
d=The amount by which velocity is decreased at each iteration of the Interpolator.

